    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`. The handler is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`), implementing the generated `OwnersApi`.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Before the handler body runs (framework layer)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires authority `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. (Only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; the `DisableSecurityConfig` profile bypasses it.)\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, interface `@Validated`) \u2014 failures raise `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400. Field constraints:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address`: `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`: `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`, `@Size(4..4)`\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Inside the handler, in execution order\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before, return the previously created owner (HTTP 200), skipping the rest entirely.\n4. **Missing-field checks** \u2014 collect blanks among `firstName`, `lastName`, then (after step 5) `address`, `city`, `telephone`; if any are missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n5. **Address normalization** *(side-effect / mutation)* \u2014 `applyAddress()` folds `addressLine1/2` into `address`, trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE. Runs between the `lastName` and `address` blank checks.\n6. **Postcode validation** \u2014 `validatePostcode(city, postcode)`: 4-digit format plus region-range check \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n7. **Future registration-date check** \u2014 if a supplied `registrationDate` is after `LocalDate.now()` \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n8. **Registration-date defaulting + business-day roll-forward** *(transformation)* \u2014 default to today if absent, then `toBusinessDay()` rolls Saturdays/Sundays/holidays forward.\n9. **Daily registration limit** \u2014 count owners already registered on that (adjusted) date; if \u2265100 \u2192 `DailyRegistrationLimitException` (429). Also sets a `bulkSignupWarning` flag if the count is >80.\n10. **City capacity check** \u2014 count owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if \u226550 \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n11. **Telephone \u2192 E.164** *(side-effect / mutation)* \u2014 `toE164()` normalizes and validates national length (+61\u21d29 digits, +1\u21d210); invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400). Writes the result back into the DTO.\n12. **Email normalization** *(side-effect / mutation)* \u2014 `normalizeEmail()` lower-cases, checks syntax, and rejects disposable domains (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail) \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (400). Writes back into the DTO.\n13. **Household duplicate check** \u2014 compute `householdId` (SHA-256 of normalized lastName + postcode); if any non-deleted owner shares it and the request did not set `sharesHousehold=true` \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException` (409).\n14. **Identity-key duplicate check** \u2014 derive an identity key from telephone|email|householdId; if any non-deleted owner matches \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Entity construction, persistence, and post-save side-effects\n\n15. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` and set derived/defaulted fields** *(transformations)*: `registrationDate`; `customerCode` (region + SHA-256, with collision de-duplication); `householdId`; `namesakeCount`; `bulkSignupWarning`; `householdSize` (= existing members + 1); `possibleDuplicate=false`; `possibleDuplicateOf=null`; `deleted=false`.\n16. **Persist** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` inserts one row into `owners` (its own transaction; the handler itself is not `@Transactional`, so the preceding reads and this write are not atomic).\n17. **Record idempotency mapping** *(side-effect)* \u2014 store `Idempotency-Key \u2192 owner.id` in the in-memory `idempotentCreates` map.\n18. **Response DTO derivations** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto()` computes (non-persisted) fields: displayName, salutation, initials, membershipNumber/level/points, checkDigit, etc.\n19. **Audit logging** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"owner created: id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026 membershipLevel=\u2026 membershipNumber=\u2026\")`.\n20. **Set `Location` header** to `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 Created**.\n\n## Notes on things that are *not* part of this path\n- No password hashing/encoding for owners \u2014 owners have no password; the `BCryptPasswordEncoder` bean exists only for user login.\n- No `@InitBinder`/`WebDataBinder`, no custom owner validator (`PetAgeValidator` is pets-only).\n- No related-entity saves, events, emails/notifications, cache eviction, or created-by/updated-by auditing.\n- The `Owner` **entity** carries its own Bean Validation (`@NotEmpty` address/city, E.164 `@Pattern` on telephone), which would apply only if the entity itself is validated (e.g. JPA pre-persist), not as part of the DTO request validation.\n\nValidation-error responses are shaped by `ExceptionControllerAdvice` (`@ControllerAdvice`), which maps each exception above to its status code and a `ProblemDetail`/`errors` body."
